 "note": "How the player's words for a person meet the words the prose first used. Original writing for Pathfinder GM (2026-09-25). groups: words that mean the same person-describing thing; the first word of a group is the one both sides are reduced to. implies: a word in a RECORD that also makes the record answer to these words (\"a crone\" is found as \"the old woman\"), one way only, so the player's \"the child\" finds a girl but the player's \"the girl\" never finds a boy. still: words that describe being somewhere rather than who somebody is, dropped from the player's phrase (\"the woman standing by the well\" is the woman at the well). Grown from real play: every search that finds nobody is written to the turn log as a population-miss, and the words it missed on are the ones this file lacks. Words that point at somebody without describing them (someone, whoever, person) are in `still` too: \"someone\" booked as a person's phrase once matched every later \"someone\" (measured live 2026-09-25).",
